                        "id":  "aerial-mycosis",
                        "title":  "Aerial Mycosis",
                        "category":  "Hazards",
                        "summary":  "A symbiotic fungus improves aerial nutrient absorption while manipulating a host\u0027s movement and behavior.",
                        "body":  [
                                     "Fungal patches on islands and abandoned ships infect mounts, Sheffels, and smaller creatures. Visible tendrils, restlessness, aggression, disorientation, lethargy, and body-borne spores indicate infection.",
                                     "Long-term magical and herbal treatment must sever the relationship, remove tissue, and monitor behavior."
                                 ],
