                        "id":  "siphon-fungus",
                        "title":  "Siphon Fungus",
                        "category":  "Hazards",
                        "summary":  "Burrowing spores root through veins and consume a host\u0027s blood until it collapses or falls.",
                        "body":  [
                                     "Skin growths, thirst, fever, blood loss, wasting, bleeding, and an audible siphoning sound mark the infection. Larger animals are especially vulnerable.",
                                     "Physical extraction and magical purging must remove roots before organs or limbs are consumed; blood-restoring medicines aid recovery."
                                 ],
