                        "title":  "Windblight",
                        "category":  "Hazards",
                        "summary":  "A damp-weather respiratory fungus infects livestock and people through spores and contaminated vegetation.",
                        "body":  [
                                     "Persistent cough, wheezing, oxygen loss, metallic taste, and growth around the mouth mark progressive lung infection in windy fogbound regions.",
                                     "Antifungal potions, respiratory aids, purification, herbs, and isolation from contaminated areas are standard treatment."
                                 ],
